BLOG=[
('how-to-edit-wedding-album-psd','How to Edit a Wedding Album PSD in Photoshop (Step-by-Step)',['Open the PSD and look at the Layers panel first. Good album templates group photo placeholders, text and decorations separately so you always know what you are editing.','Drag a photo onto the document, place it directly above a placeholder layer and press Alt+Ctrl+G (Option+Cmd+G on Mac) to clip it inside the mask.','Use Free Transform (Ctrl+T) to scale and position each photo. Recent Photoshop versions keep proportions by default; hold Shift to unlock them.','Edit names and dates with the Type tool, and recolour shapes with Hue/Saturation or Color Fill adjustment layers so the original artwork stays untouched.','Export a full-resolution JPG for the print lab and keep the layered PSD so you can handle client corrections later.']),
('12x36-album-size-guide','12x36 Album Size Guide: Pixels, DPI and Print Settings',['A 12x36 inch spread at 300 DPI is 10800x3600 pixels. At 150 DPI it is 5400x1800 pixels, which many labs accept for album sheets.','Higher DPI gives sharper detail but larger files. For most wedding albums viewed at arm\'s length, 200–300 DPI is plenty.','Leave around 0.25 inch of bleed on every edge and keep faces and text well away from the centre fold.','Most digital labs print from RGB files. Only convert to CMYK if your printer specifically asks for it.']),
('karizma-album-design-tips','10 Karizma Album Design Tips for Photo Studios',['Tell a story by arranging spreads in event order, from preparations to the reception.','Give each spread one hero photo and a few supporting shots instead of crowding the page.','Repeat a small colour palette across the album for a premium, consistent look.','Use matching backgrounds from the same set so pages flow naturally.','Check every spread at 100% zoom before sending it for printing.']),
('birthday-album-psd-ideas','Birthday and Baby Album PSD Ideas Clients Love',['Bright pastel backgrounds and playful fonts suit kids\' albums best.','Add milestone pages such as first smile, first steps and the first birthday cake.','Include a family page with grandparents to make the album a lasting keepsake.','Keep text short so the photos stay the hero of every page.']),
('choose-album-background-psd','How to Choose the Right Album Background PSD',['Match the background mood to the event: gold and maroon for weddings, soft pastels for baby albums.','Choose backgrounds with low detail behind faces so the subject stands out.','Make sure the background resolution matches your album size before you start designing.']),
('clipping-masks-explained','Clipping Masks Explained for Album Designers',['A clipping mask shows the layer above only where the layer below has pixels. Album templates use this to keep photos inside frames.','To clip, place the photo directly above the frame shape and press Alt+Ctrl+G.','To swap a photo, select the old photo layer, delete it and clip a new one in the same position.','If a photo disappears, check that it sits immediately above the mask layer in the Layers panel.']),
('organise-photos-before-album-design','How to Organise Photos Before Designing an Album',['Start by culling: remove blinks, duplicates and out-of-focus shots.','Group the remaining photos by event, such as ceremony, portraits, family and reception.','Pick hero photos for each group first, then supporting images.','Rename folders in event order so you can design spreads quickly.']),
('album-colour-correction-tips','Colour Correction Tips for Wedding Album Photos',['Correct white balance first so skin tones look natural.','Use Curves for contrast rather than pushing brightness sliders.','Keep a consistent look across the album by applying the same preset or adjustment group.','Check skin tones on a calibrated monitor before printing.']),
('album-cover-design-guide','Album Cover Design Guide: Making a Strong First Impression',['The cover is the first thing clients see, so use your best couple portrait.','Keep the title, names and date simple and readable.','Choose a cover design whose colours match the inside pages.','Leave safe margins so nothing important is lost in binding.']),
('print-ready-psd-checklist','Print-Ready PSD Checklist Before Sending to the Lab',['Confirm the canvas size and DPI match the album size you ordered.','Check that every photo is sharp at 100% zoom.','Make sure text is spelled correctly, especially names and dates.','Flatten a copy and save it as a high-quality JPG or TIFF as the lab requires.','Keep the layered PSD archived for reprints.']),
('fonts-for-wedding-albums','Choosing Fonts for Wedding Album Designs',['Pair one decorative script font with one clean sans-serif for balance.','Avoid using more than two or three fonts in one album.','Make names larger and supporting text smaller for a clear hierarchy.','If a PSD uses a missing font, Photoshop will ask you to replace it; choose a similar style.']),
('speed-up-album-design-workflow','How to Speed Up Your Album Design Workflow',['Build a library of templates and backgrounds you trust.','Use Photoshop actions for repeated steps like resizing and sharpening.','Design spreads in batches by event instead of jumping around.','Keep a checklist so nothing is missed before printing.']),
('pre-wedding-album-ideas','Pre-Wedding Album Design Ideas',['Pre-wedding shoots allow more creative, cinematic layouts.','Use large full-bleed photos and minimal text.','Choose backgrounds and colours that match the shoot location.','Tell a simple love story from first look to final pose.']),
('muslim-wedding-album-design','Designing a Muslim Wedding Album: Layout Ideas',['Plan spreads around key moments such as the Nikah, family portraits and the Walima.','Elegant geometric patterns and soft golds suit many Muslim wedding albums.','Keep layouts respectful and balanced, with space for family group photos.','Use matching backgrounds from one set for a unified feel.']),
('christian-wedding-album-design','Christian Wedding Album Layout Ideas',['Cover the church ceremony, ring exchange and reception in story order.','White, ivory and soft floral themes work beautifully.','Give the vows and ring moments their own spreads.','Finish with a candid reception page and a couple portrait.']),
('hindu-wedding-album-design','Hindu Wedding Album Design Tips',['Plan spreads for Haldi, Mehndi, the main ceremony and the reception.','Rich maroon, red and gold themes suit traditional albums.','Use ornate borders for ritual pages and cleaner layouts for portraits.','Keep a family page for elders and relatives.']),
('photoshop-shortcuts-album-design','25 Photoshop Shortcuts Every Album Designer Should Know',['Ctrl+T for Free Transform, Ctrl+J to duplicate a layer and Alt+Ctrl+G to create a clipping mask.','Ctrl+G groups layers and Ctrl+Shift+N creates a new layer.','Hold Space to pan and use Ctrl+0 to fit the canvas on screen.','Press D then X to reset and swap foreground and background colours.']),
('rgb-vs-cmyk-for-albums','RGB vs CMYK for Album Printing',['Most photo labs use RGB workflows, so keep your album files in RGB unless told otherwise.','CMYK has a smaller colour range and can make bright colours look dull.','Always ask your lab for their preferred colour profile.','Soft-proof in Photoshop to preview printed colours.']),
('studio-backdrop-psd-guide','How to Use Studio Backdrop PSDs',['Studio backdrop PSDs let you place portraits on a clean, professional background.','Cut out the subject with Select Subject and refine the edge with Select and Mask.','Match lighting direction and add a soft shadow for realism.','Adjust backdrop colours with adjustment layers to suit the outfit.']),
('album-design-mistakes','8 Album Design Mistakes to Avoid',['Putting faces across the centre fold.','Using too many photos on a single spread.','Mixing unrelated background styles.','Using low-resolution photos that print blurry.','Forgetting to double-check spelling of names.']),
('12x30-vs-12x36-album','12x30 vs 12x36 Album: Which Size to Choose?',['12x36 spreads are wider and suit panoramic, cinematic layouts.','12x30 is slightly more compact and often more affordable to print.','Check which sizes your lab offers before choosing templates.','Keep the same size throughout one album for a consistent book.']),
('how-to-download-psd-files','How to Download and Open PSD Files from FreeStudioPSD',['Open any design page and click the Free Download button.','Wait for the short countdown, then click the Google Drive link.','The file downloads as a ZIP; extract it with your system\'s built-in tool or 7-Zip.','Open the PSD in Adobe Photoshop CC or a compatible editor.']),
('baby-album-design-guide','Baby Album Design Guide for Studios',['Use soft colours, simple shapes and gentle fonts.','Plan pages by month or milestone.','Add small details like hand and foot prints.','Leave space for family notes and dates.']),
('engagement-album-layouts','Engagement Album Layout Ideas',['Focus on the ring, the couple and family blessings.','Use bright, celebratory backgrounds.','Combine close-up detail shots with wide group photos.','Keep text minimal, with names and the date only.']),
('start-album-design-business','How to Start an Album Design Service from Home',['Learn Photoshop basics: layers, masks and colour correction.','Build a portfolio using free templates and practice photos.','Offer fast turnaround and clear pricing to local studios.','Keep improving with new templates and design trends.']),
]
